# !! DO NOT TYPE A REAL VALUE INTO THIS FILE. It is committed and this repository is
# !! PUBLIC. The placeholder below is deliberately not blank, so that a value left
# !! unreplaced fails loudly at authentication instead of silently becoming an empty
# !! credential. Copy this file first; edit only the copy.
#
# TEMPLATE — committed. Copy it, do not edit it in place:
#
#   cp apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/env.secret.openclaw-metrics.example \
#      apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.openclaw-metrics
#   $EDITOR apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.openclaw-metrics
#   ./scripts/encrypt-env-files.sh \
#     apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.openclaw-metrics
#
# All from the REPO ROOT — the script resolves its arguments against your current
# directory. It takes a single file (as above, encrypting only that one) or a directory
# (encrypting every .env* file under it, which also rewrites the other .encrypted files
# in this directory — harmless, but it makes for a noisier diff).
#
# Run that last command YOURSELF rather than asking the agent to. The agent must never
# create, read or write the real path: on 2026-08-29 two credentials were burned because
# the real file was in the agent's read-set and the harness reported the change including
# the secret line, even though the edit happened outside the agent's tools.
#
# The copy is gitignored (`.env*`); only the `.encrypted` output is committed.

# HALF OF A PAIR. This is the bearer token Prometheus presents when scraping OpenClaw's
# /api/diagnostics/prometheus endpoint, which requires operator.read auth. The other half
# is openclaw_gateway_token in apps/production/olya/.env.secret.olya.encrypted — the value
# the gateway itself reads as OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN — and the two MUST hold the identical
# value. Copy it from over there; do not generate a fresh value here.
#
# The key is lowercase because it becomes the mounted filename: the Secret
# `openclaw-metrics-auth` (kustomization.yaml) is mounted at /etc/prometheus/secrets/openclaw
# by server.extraSecretMounts in helmrelease.yaml, and the openclaw scrape job reads
# credentials_file: /etc/prometheus/secrets/openclaw/openclaw_gateway_token. A file rather
# than an inline credential because extraScrapeConfigs renders into a ConfigMap, which is
# not a Secret and is readable by anyone who can read the Prometheus config.
#
# Prometheus applies strings.TrimSpace to the file contents, so trailing whitespace here is
# invisible while the gateway treats its env var as exact — whitespace on one side only is a
# 401 that reads as a wrong token. Paste the value with no quotes and no surrounding
# whitespace.
openclaw_gateway_token=<REPLACE-ME-same-value-as-openclaw_gateway_token>
